  "evidenceBoundary": {
    "exact": "Selected code windows and exact exception-table parent triples establish constructor, parameter lookup and hit-writer bodies.",
    "direct": "The complex constructor stores its separate shape in masked actor userdata +8. Parameter index zero reads that shape; positive indices subtract one and enumerate actor shapes. The common constructor now calls a factory helper, whose successful creation path invokes actor attachShape and returns the shape only when attachment succeeds. The current hit writer compares the returned shape with actor enumeration using a one-based result. Unavailable face and successful triangle/remap paths remain distinct; neither exposes a geometry pointer or concrete vtable.",
    "conditional": "Positive descriptor candidates exclude the separately stored complexMesh record. Successful attachment, skipped constructors, later attachment/removal, actor shape reordering and exact mesh geometry remain independent conditions. Matching parameter tuples never prove geometry.",
    "unresolved": "Actual per-constructor success, exact returned-shape geometry and live attachment history are not supplied by this static contract."
  }
